  "intro": "That's a wrap on the 40th Anniversary season. The 68 brought it home at Tri-City's Fall Classic Championship Night — second in the main, 59 points on the night — and closes out the 2026 VMRA championship on 616, 36 clear of the field.\n\nThe fight for second went right down to the wire. Kahl Cheth won the main in the 23 and had the biggest night of anyone, 63 points, to pull dead level with Jason Quatsoe's 8 on 580. Tied on points, the tiebreak goes to the main event — Cheth's win puts the 23 second, Quatsoe's 8 third. Vince Conwell ran third in the main in the Northwest Concrete Cutting car and holds fourth at 539, just 4 ahead of Shane Strimple's 57 on 535.\n\nRookie of the Year goes to Bart Hecter Jr on 287, with Jesse Boczar second on 185. Thanks to every driver, crew, track and fan who made year 40 one to remember. Points stay with the car, not the driver.",
